# act (nektos/act) runner-label → image mappings for this repo.
#
# Our CI jobs run on a self-hosted runner declared as
# `runs-on: [self-hosted, Linux, X64]` inside the shared CI container
# `ghcr.io/superfield-ai/ci-runner:latest`. act needs each of those labels
# mapped to a local image so it schedules the job against the same container CI
# uses — making a local `act` run execute the *unmodified* workflow YAML in the
# same environment as CI. See evals/README.md ("Running an eval locally").
#
# Only repo-wide-correct defaults belong here. Run-specific flags
# (--pull=false, --artifact-server-path) stay on the command line.
#
# Prereq/limitation: the ci-runner image has no `node`, so act stops at the
# first JS action (actions/cache, upload-artifact). Tracked in #810.
-P self-hosted=ghcr.io/superfield-ai/ci-runner:latest
-P Linux=ghcr.io/superfield-ai/ci-runner:latest
-P X64=ghcr.io/superfield-ai/ci-runner:latest
